{#- The heading the off-scene cast directory opens with, shared by its two tier
    sections (off_scene_cast_active.j2, off_scene_cast_known.j2).

    A file of its own rather than a copy in each of them: the directory used to
    be one template and one section, and splitting it so the two tiers could be
    measured separately (#2) must not turn a single line of instruction into
    two that can drift apart.

    NEITHER section renders it. `Section.heading` names this template and
    `context.assemble._render_sections` prepends it to whichever member of the
    group actually produced text first, so the directory opens with exactly one
    copy however the reader's prompt layout orders or disables its halves.
    Deciding that in a template is what #423 was: "am I first?" is a question
    about the merged, enabled layout, and a template can only see the data. -#}
